WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:12.623
Projects are for work with a start, an end, and a goal: a new store, a menu launch, a catering job. In this video, you’ll start a project with Assist, and follow one on its dashboard and plan.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:23.236
Open Projects. Each card shows the goal, the dates, how far along the milestones are, and what’s next. Filter to active ones, yours, or completed.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:28.628
Projects can be open to the company, or private to their owners, like this paused one.

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:36.832
Click New project, and give it a name and dates. Ask Assist, and it drafts the goals, milestones and deliverables for you to check.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:44.797
Every project gets its own dashboard: how much is done, open and overdue work, and what’s due in the next seven days.

00:00:45.233 --> 00:00:55.516
Below, work by person, by status and by type, and what’s been finished each week. Explain has AI sum it up, and Change with AI rearranges it for you.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:05.140
Goals and plan holds the goals, the milestones with their due dates, and the deliverables, each ticked off as it’s done. Click Edit plan to change it.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:12.491
And the Tickets tab lists the project’s own tickets, with their own key, so everything for the opening lives in one place.

